usage: capcov [-h] [--quiet]
              {flows,outcomes,features,discover,observe,reconcile,gate,report} ...

capcov command line: discover, observe, reconcile, gate, report. `discover`
and `observe` both always run. There is no static-only mode and no threshold
that switches between them -- that was a rejected design, and what it amounted
to was a tool that sometimes does not work with the answer bolted on beside
it.

positional arguments:
  {flows,outcomes,features,discover,observe,reconcile,gate,report}
    flows               source obligations, flow planning, and browser outcome
                        evidence
    outcomes            scoped behavior obligations and fresh pytest evidence
    features            FODA feature-model validation, configuration check,
                        coverage rollup
    discover            static: entities, surfaces, bindings
    observe             runtime: run the exercises with the probe
    reconcile           the four-way diff
    gate                fail on anything unexplained
    report              human-readable coverage table

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --quiet
